veats enable fine-grained restriction (route, method, TTL, budget), reducing blast radius and enabling safe delegation."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-gray-300","children":"Reduced Trust Dependencies:"}]," ","Authorization is cryptographic, not reliant on a centralized user database. Optional state can be used for metering/quotas without requiring PII."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-gray-800","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-300 mb-3","children":"What SatGate is (and isn't)"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"text-gray-500 text-sm space-y-1","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"text-green-400","children":"✓ Zero Trust PEP for API access (request-level verification + least privilege)"}],["$","li",null,{"className":"text-green-400","children":"✓ Complements existing security stack (WAF/CDN, rate limiting, SIEM)"}],["$","li",null,{"className":"text-yellow-400","children":"⚠ Not a full Zero Trust program (identity governance, device posture, microsegmentation)"}]]}]]}]]}]
